    "body": "I guess maybe I misunderstood the original attack. It's not the fact that the page navigated that we consider sensitive. It's the URL the page navigated to.\r\n\r\nThat can be mitigated, as Chromium has done, by avoiding the same-URL-replace behavior when the initiator is cross-origin: https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=1208614 (although I don't think that bug is public).",
