    "created_at": "2022-03-18T10:12:15Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-03-18T10:12:15Z",
    "body": "I am wondering if there is additional information being revealed by the joint history state compared to listening to onload events from the iframes, beyond the potential URL issue you point to. For example, if a cross-origin iframe were to navigate in a manner that causes the current history entry to be replaced rather than a new one being added, this is something that could be seen through the evolution of the joint history but not by listening to the iframe load events, which I think would be similar in both cases.\r\n\r\nAdditionally, the history API is accessible from iframes I believe, which makes it possible for an iframe to leak data from siblings iframes right? Which wouldn't be possible from just listening to onload callbacks.\r\n\r\nSo overall, it would seem to me that the history API has XSite leak capabilities that go beyond listening to load callbacks. Since it also seems that it is not the most handy API anyway, it would be good if the XSite leak capabilities were mitigated.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
